text.section:
A separate citation which has been approved in the manner prescribed in subsection A shall be used for violations of §§ 46.2-1122 through 46.2-1127 and 46.2-1130. The citation shall be directed to the owner, operator or other person responsible for the overweight violation, and shall advise him of:

The nature of the violation charged against him;


The amount of monetary fees, penalties, and damages that may be assessed for violations;


The requirement that he either pay the fees, penalties, and damages in full or deliver a notice of his intent to contest the charge to the Department;


The procedures and time limits for making the payments or contesting such charge, which shall include the trial date, which shall in no event be earlier than 60 days after the violation; and


The consequences of a failure to timely pay or contest the charge.

A separate citation that has been approved in the manner prescribed in subsection A shall be used for violations of § 46.2-613.1. The citation shall be directed to the owner, operator, or other person responsible for the violation and shall advise him of:

The nature of the violation charged against him;


The amount of monetary fees and penalties that may be assessed for violations;


The requirement that he either pay the fee and penalties in full or deliver a notice of his intent to contest the charge to the Department;


The procedures and time limits for making the payments or contesting such charge which shall include the trial date, which shall in no event be earlier than 60 days after the violation; and


The consequences of a failure to timely pay or contest the charge.
